# node_modules IS committed, deliberately.
#
# Claude Code does not run `npm install` when a plugin is installed from a
# marketplace, and three dependencies (yaml, ajv, proper-lockfile) are used on
# the module-load path -- lib/discovery.mjs imports `yaml` before anything else
# runs. Without them vendored, a plugin install throws "Cannot find module
# 'yaml'" on first use, which is a worse failure than 4 MB of repo weight.
#
# Bundling with `bun build` was tried and produces 4 files instead of 798, but
# the entry points would then be dist/*.js while SKILL.md, the launchd plist and
# every doc reference the .mjs sources -- a build artifact that must be
# regenerated on every change is exactly the drift this repo exists to detect.
#
# Regenerate with: npm ci --omit=dev
# runtime state — not source
state.json
state.json.bak
heartbeat
.lock-target
*.log
.DS_Store
.code-review-graph/
watcher.log
*.log.*.gz
# derived index — disposable, rebuilt in <1s via `node index.mjs --rebuild`
index.db
index.db-journal
index.db-wal
index.db-shm

# Lifecycle event log — machine-local history of promote/demote/reap. Like
# index.db this is per-machine state, not source.
SKILLS_LIFECYCLE.jsonl
